fysetc-5inch-dsi (1.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Panel driver: register an on/off backlight device (max_brightness 1).
    The Fysetc MCU only switches the backlight (REG_PWM 0x00 off, 0xff on,
    other values ignored). The DRM core switches it with the panel, so
    screen blanking (DPMS) turns the backlight off and the user setting
    survives a wake.
  * Repository renamed to armbian-fysetc-5inch-display.

 -- niklas389 <niklas389@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000

fysetc-5inch-dsi (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Touch poller: speak the Fysetc panel MCU's actual read protocol. The MCU
    at 0x38 emulates an FT5x06, but only the first byte of a read comes from
    the selected register; further bytes come from a 3-byte ring whose
    pointer is never reset. Read TD_STATUS with 1-byte and points with 4-byte
    reads, detect the ring phase from the data. Fixes phantom touches and
    missing touch input.
  * Invert both touch axes by default (-X -Y), as the panel reports them.
  * Probe mode (-p) prints TD_STATUS, raw point records and decoded points.

 -- niklas389 <niklas389@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0000

fysetc-5inch-dsi (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package display overlay, DKMS panel driver and touch poller as one .deb.
  * Touch poller: discard invalid controller frames (device mode, TD_STATUS,
    duplicate IDs, out-of-range coordinates), debounce new contacts, emit only
    changed values, release contacts on persistent read errors or garbage,
    set axis resolution, refuse to run when a kernel driver owns 0x38, and
    add a probe mode (-p) for raw register dumps.
  * Panel driver build: build against the kernel DKMS targets instead of
    the running kernel.

 -- niklas389 <niklas389@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
